{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794229116,"nonce":"xk2g1R7po+3YFk96fwoFeA0A0fk=","title":"A window resize rebuilds the whole tree","message":"The windowed runner sets `needs_rebuild` on every `Resized` event, so a live\nresize runs the app's build closure and a full tree build per event, even\nwhen the UI fills the window with `w_full`/`h_full` and reads nothing from the\nwindow size. On the russl toy a full build is ~15 ms (after the class-matching\nfix), so a live resize runs well under the display rate.\n\nA resize changes the viewport, not the structure: relayout should be enough\nunless the build reads `ctx.width`/`ctx.height`. Options: track whether the\nbuild read the window size and rebuild only then, or offer a viewport signal\nthe build can bind to instead.","files":null}]}